READ RULE E CAREFULLY. It is the strongest thing a PER-POSITION scorer
can do: test this message's payload against both thresholds, ignoring
all state. In v3 the equivalent rule scored 100% because compressorOn
was a write-once latch. If E is now well under 100%, then v4 genuinely
REQUIRES tracking compressorOn across the prefix, i.e. it is a real
benchmark and the surrogate finally has something to learn.

